      "timestamp_sec": 338,
      "why": "Grounds review in accountability rather than code quality."
    },
    {
      "text": "I think right now it's switching. Most people are starting to use CLIs more often than IDEs.",
      "timestamp_sec": 428,
      "why": "An empirical claim about tooling adoption from someone shipping both."
    },
    {
      "text": "When we released this, it actually went a little bit viral. We got tens of thousands of downloads.",
      "timestamp_sec": 468,
      "why": "Reported number on Kiro's launch."
    },
    {
      "text": "But I don't want this to be a half-hour pitch for Kiro. You can do this process spec-driven development without Kiro and there's a few few ways.",
      "timestamp_sec": 504,
      "why": "Explicitly decouples the practice from the product."
    },
    {
      "text": "Now, you're probably thinking is this spec only good for greenfield brand new projects? And I would say absolutely not. I've seen existing apps that are years old have dozens and dozens of these different spec files in them.",
      "timestamp_sec": 584,
      "why": "Directly rebuts the most common objection to spec-first workflows."
    },
    {
      "text": "these are really good for when you're doing in-depth features, when you need your project needs a little more upfront planning, uh and you just want to build things in a structured way.",
      "timestamp_sec": 619,
      "why": "Scopes where the overhead pays off."
    },
    {
      "text": "Now, this is at the point I would highly recommend, if you're trying this at home, to stop and go in and update it with your knowledge and expertise and taste to exactly what you're looking for. Because it's only as good as what you put in.",
      "timestamp_sec": 694,
      "why": "Pinpoints the single highest-leverage human intervention in the flow."
    },
    {
      "text": "Uh it also has something called property-based tests in them, which are tests that are against the requirements document and design document.",
      "timestamp_sec": 732,
      "why": "Links verification back to the spec artifacts, closing the loop."
    },
    {
      "text": "I tell it, \"Please take the top four tasks, put them at the top, and create an MVP for me first.\" So that way I can actually see it working.",
      "timestamp_sec": 732,
      "why": "Actionable technique any listener can copy."
    },
    {
      "text": "I really think MCP is still maturing. There's a lot uh a long road ahead for it, especially with some of the security stuff it's doing. I would keep an eye out for MCP",
